<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rasarnava Sudhakara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rasarnava Sudhakara is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> treatise on dramaturgy and poetics attributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarvajna-singabhupala">Sarvajna Singabhupala</a>, a Recherla <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayaka</a> king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rachakonda">Rachakonda</a> in the 14th century. It analyses rasa, the aesthetic emotion evoked by drama, together with characters, plot construction and the types of plays. It is one of the important later works in the Sanskrit tradition of dramatic theory.</p></div>
